-- title:
--   Irreducible polynomials whose real loci correspond under $z\mapsto az+b$ generate the same ideal after substitution
-- statement:
--   For a polynomial $R\in\mathbb C[X,Y]$, let $Z(R)=\{z\in\mathbb C:\ R(z,\bar z)=0\}$ be its real locus in the complex coordinates $X=z$, $Y=\bar z$. For a real polynomial $f(x,y)$ rewritten in these coordinates, $Z$ is the zero set of $f$ in $\mathbb R^2=\mathbb C$.
--
--   Let $P,Q\in\mathbb C[X,Y]$ be irreducible polynomials whose real loci $Z(P)$ and $Z(Q)$ are infinite. Let $a,b\in\mathbb C$ with $a\ne0$, and suppose that the similarity $S(z)=az+b$ maps $Z(Q)$ onto $Z(P)$, that is, $S(Z(Q))=Z(P)$. Let $\sigma$ be the automorphism of the $\mathbb C$-algebra $\mathbb C[X,Y]$ given by $\sigma(R)(X,Y)=R(aX+b,\ \bar aY+\bar b)$, the substitution of $S$ in these coordinates. Then the ideal generated by $P$ is the image under $\sigma^{-1}$ of the ideal generated by $Q$:
--
--   $$(P)=\sigma^{-1}\bigl((Q)\bigr)=\Bigl(Q\Bigl(\frac{X-b}{a},\ \frac{Y-\bar b}{\bar a}\Bigr)\Bigr).$$
--
--   Equivalently, $P$ is a nonzero constant multiple of $Q\bigl(\frac{X-b}{a},\frac{Y-\bar b}{\bar a}\bigr)$.
--
--   In the check of Remark 5 this is how a similarity between real loci yields an isomorphism of the coordinate rings $\mathbb C[X,Y]/(P)\cong\mathbb C[X,Y]/(Q)$, hence of the function fields, to which the invariance of the genus applies.
--
--   **Formalization Note**: $\mathbb C[X,Y]$ is `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) ℂ` and $Z(R)$ is a subset of $\mathbb C$; the right-hand side is the image (`Ideal.map`) of the ideal $(Q)$ under $\sigma^{-1}$.
-- source:
--   C. Perassi, Sharp symmetry bounds for real algebraic curves (note): lemma of the formalization, for Remark 5, p. 4, https://github.com/carlok/curve-symmetry-lean/blob/d99bc17a1c397956c05d7417de50f9beed56580f/sharp_symmetry_bounds.pdf. Lean: https://github.com/carlok/curve-symmetry-lean/blob/d99bc17a1c397956c05d7417de50f9beed56580f/lean/QuarticComparison.lean (C. Perassi)

